{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"12f5fb81e249020b7db5ff10c7989cc40a995f34d4501f96e9a382df4cd54e16","digest":{"component_or_area":"alert_store / BindingRepository lifecycle alerts","key_entities":["alert_store.is_deduped","alert_store.append","BindingRepository.alert","binding_repository.py:304","binding_lifecycle.py","timestamp_ns","bridge_alerts","is_deduped"],"problem_keywords":["alert deduplication","timestamp omission","lifecycle alerts","binding repository","dedup window ineffective"],"propositions":["BindingRepository.alert() builds records without timestamp_ns, causing alert_store.is_deduped to default ts to 0, which always exceeds the 24h window and suppression never fires.","Multiple BindingRepository passes over a corrupt bindings-retired.json append duplicate binding-retired-file-corrupt records indefinitely rather than deduplicating within the window.","The fix centralizes timestamp_ns ownership in alert_store.append so caller-supplied values win and all existing stampers remain unchanged while unstamped callers gain the field.","Records already persisted without timestamp_ns must remain readable via is_deduped's get() default to 0, treating them as out-of-window and never throwing."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787688540816749001,"uuid":"3881b5ed-8dc9-400c-9500-dc352479fe45"}